details.contract:
app/bin/codegraph.ts keeps its shebang, its lazy `const { main } = await import("../src/index")` import and its `process.exit(await main(requested, argv))` tail. Replace the four-name MODES allow-list with `const RESERVED = ["mcp", "worker"] as const`, and make the entry accept either a reserved mode or a tool name:

const argv = process.argv.slice(2);
const requested = argv[0] ?? "mcp";

When `requested` is `--help`, `-h` or `help`, print USAGE to stdout and exit 0 without importing the kernel. Otherwise call main(requested, argv) and, when it returns 2 (the usage exit code), print USAGE to stderr and exit 2. Every other code is passed through unchanged. The bin file must not import #shared/* or the tool registry; the usage banner is a literal that names the modes `mcp` and `worker` and the seven tools `status`, `summary`, `trace`, `search`, `impact`, `expand`, `index`, plus one example line `cgraph trace 'handleRequest' --depth 1` and one `cgraph mcp --repo-root /path/to/repo`.

Keep the file under ~60 lines and keep the comment explaining why the import is lazy.
